<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trophonius</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oracle of Trophonius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trophonius was a Greek hero worshipped at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livadeia">Lebadea</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, where his underground oracle was one of the most famous in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. According to legend he and his brother Agamedes built the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> at Delphi. Those consulting him underwent purification rites before descending into a narrow chamber, from which they were said to emerge terrified; Pausanias, who consulted the oracle, left a detailed description.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trophonius.jpg" alt="Trophonius" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Todd from Xinzheng, China · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Greece_Limestone_Votive_Relief,_350-325_BC_(27880856203).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
